261"}, {"study_label": "MitoQ preeclampsia (registry)", "outcome": "Placental function", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT07229261"}, {"study_label": "MitoQ preeclampsia (registry)", "outcome": "Pregnancy prolongation", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT07229261"}], "gap_cells": [{"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42794697", "42630618"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42495453", "42479041"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42535808"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "septic cardiomyopathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42460027"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "preeclampsia", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT07229261"]}, {"intervention": "Mitochondria-targeted agents (pooled trials)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42440741"]}, {"intervention": "Mitochondria-targeted nanomedicines", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42022751"]}, {"intervention": "Mitochondria-targeted approaches (narrative reviews)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 4, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["40845481", "41595638", "42746169", "42609595"]}, {"intervention": "Urolithin A", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42616901", "42432192"]}, {"intervention": "Luteolin", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42013553"]}, {"intervention": "Calhex231", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42748783"]}, {"intervention": "Elamipretide", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["40816230"]}, {"intervention": "Elamipretide / deoxynucleoside / sildenafil (commentary)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["42229401"]}, {"intervention": "PMD interventional therapies (ClinicalTrials.gov survey)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42361626"]}, {"intervention": "PMD therapeutic compounds (review)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42650043"]}, {"intervention": "Exercise", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42770008"]}, {"intervention": "TazPM (Taz2 D75H) knock-in mouse model", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42783548"]}, {"intervention": "AAV2-ND6 allotopic gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42709484"]}, {"intervention": "rAAV2/2-ND4 gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42131170"]}, {"intervention": "m.11778G>A genetic architecture (no intervention)", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["42632451"]}, {"intervention": "NAD+ supplementation (NR/NMN)", "disease": "unclear", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42489969"]}, {"intervention": "Restorin NR (crystalline NR fumarate)", "disease": "aging (murine model)", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42582917"]}, {"intervention": "Dimethyl malonate", "disease": "septic cardiomyopathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42805426"]}], "insights": ["Chronic heart failure: the only meta-analysis with head-to-head effect estimates (mitochondria-targeted agents vs control) shows significant benefits — LVEF SMD 0.42 (95% CI 0.31-0.53), NYHA improvement RR 2.38, all-cause mortality RR 0.62, HF hospitalizations RR 0.60 — but the control arm is not confirmed to be GDMT, so this is not a true mito-vs-GDMT contrast; the standard arm's own effect was not reported, and no RCT-level individual trial data appear in the set. [42440741]", "Primary mitochondrial diseases: broad pipeline, thin results — a ClinicalTrials.gov survey counted 159 registered studies (110 interventional) while reporting that 'several well-designed late-stage trials have yielded negative or inconclusive outcomes'; a meta-analysis of antioxidant/metabolic therapies found results 'largely negative or mixed'; the MitoQ meta could not assess efficacy at all; only four therapies have achieved regulatory authorization, while standard of care remains supportive care with no approved disease-modifying therapy. [42361626, 42630618, 42794697, 42650043]", "Primary mitochondrial diseases: the only positive patient-level signal is a single elamipretide case report (n=1, observational) with sustained clinical improvement and inactivation on the heart-transplant list — far too weak to establish benefit over supportive-care SOC; a commentary adds a speculative sildenafil-for-Leigh-syndrome suggestion with no supporting data. [40816230, 42229401]", "LHON (SOC: idebenone): the best evidence is preclinical AAV2-ND6 allotopic gene therapy (significant visual-function restoration in ND6P25L mice) and a Phase-1 meta-analysis for rAAV2/2-ND4 (BCVA significantly improved, but responder rates did not significantly increase; no treatment-related mortality); the MitoQ meta shows no clear visual effect; no study in the set compares any mito-targeted agent head-to-head against idebenone. [42709484, 42131170, 42535808]", "Preclinical consistency without clinical proof: urolithin A (2 studies), MitoQ (diabetic cardiomyopathy, septic cardiomyopathy), luteolin, dimethyl malonate, and Calhex231 all trend positive on surrogate cardiac outcomes (remodeling, diastolic function, fibrosis, oxidative stress, ferroptosis); only Calhex231 reported significant effects (LVEDD/EF/fibrosis in a rat MI model) — all other preclinical items lack reported p-values, so these are direction-only, preclinical-tier signals, not established efficacy. [42432192, 42616901, 42479041, 42460027, 42013553, 42805426, 42748783]", "No standard-arm markers could be emitted at all: no record has is_standard_of_care=true and none reports a comparator arm's own effect, so the 'vs SOC' side of this comparison is defined only by the SOC map (supportive care for PMD; idebenone for LHON; GDMT for HF) plus the pooled meta's vs-control contrasts; the MitoQ preeclampsia trial (N=80) is registry pipeline activity with no posted results, coded as unclear, not evidence of effect. [42440741, NCT07229261]"]}